KNOWNBUG
output_port_part_select_driver1.sv
--bound 10
^\[main\.p0\] always main\.counter != 5: REFUTED$
^\[main\.p1\] always main\.v != 5: REFUTED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
An output port of a child module connected to a part-select of a parent net
(.o(v[3:0])) is not recognised as a driver of those bits.  EBMC fills the
part-select with a time-invariant nondet(main.v) and additionally constrains
it to equal the port, so the two constraints conflict and no trace longer
than one step survives.  Both properties are therefore wrongly reported as
PROVED, even p0, which does not mention v.

--show-trans shows two conflicting constraints on v:
  main.v == { 4'b0000, nondet(main.v)[3:0] }
  main.v[3:0] == main.s.o

Both properties should be REFUTED: the counter reaches 5 after 5 cycles.
Driving the same bits with "assign v[3:0] = counter[3:0];" instead of the
child output port correctly refutes both.

See https://github.com/diffblue/hw-cbmc/issues/2251
